!! Getting Started

This plugin works best when your wiki already contains literature tiddlers, colleague tiddlers, or both.

!! Basic setup

* Install the plugin and the BibTeX plugin if you plan to import BibTeX entries.
* Run TiddlyWiki on Node.js so the plugin routes are available.
* Optional: install the [[PubConnector browser extension|https://github.com/byzheng/PubConnector]] if you use browser-assisted workflows such as Google Scholar capture or image handling.

!! Core tiddler types

* `Colleague` tiddlers: person profiles used for publication sync.
* `bibtex-entry` tiddlers: literature records, usually DOI-backed.
* Domain tiddlers: concept pages used by article domain auto-linking.

!! Common fields

For colleague tiddlers, tw-pubconnector can use these fields when present:

* `orcid`
* `openalex`
* `google-scholar`
* `researcherid`
* `scopus`
* `url`

For literature tiddlers, the most important field is:

* `bibtex-doi`

!! Recommended first steps

# Create or clean up your colleague tiddlers.
# Check the settings in [[$:/plugins/bangyou/tw-pubconnector/settings/authoring]].
# Import a few papers with BibTeX.
# Open [[tutorial/article-reader]] and [[tutorial/widgets]] to add reader and dashboard features.